# E00 Agents4: parallel; each agent writes 3 messages in each of turns 1 to 3, then stops in turn 4 and, in the C#,
# still sends 3 messages (kept by the port), which the writer prints only if they reach it before its last
# activation: 45 to 60 lines. Compared: the 45 messages of turns 1 to 3 (each agent in order), and the bounds of the late
# ones (none in fixed).
cover all
fact message ^\[(a\d) -> writer\]: Agent (a\d) turn (\d) index (\d)$
fact early ^\[(a\d) -> writer\]: Agent a\d turn ([1-3]) index (\d)$
fact late ^\[(a\d) -> writer\]: Agent a\d turn (4) index (\d)$
optional late
same early bag
same early seq by 0
check early count == 45
check late count in [0,15]
check message count in [45,60]
fact error (Exception|out of range)
optional error
check error count == 0
